Third-party material in the baud-font crate

The licence of baud-font is LICENSE. This file lists the material from other
projects that files in this crate carry: for each, the files by their paths
in this crate, the licence it keeps, and where the notice that licence asks
for is. It is generated from baud's record of third-party files, in its
repository at https://github.com/baud-terminal/baud, whose THIRD_PARTY.md
lists every such file there.

Tables generated from the Unicode Character Database and Unicode's emoji
data files: grapheme clusters, widths, canonical composition,
default-ignorable code points, bidirectional classes and brackets, cursive
joining and the Arabic presentation forms, line breaking, emoji
presentation, case folding and decomposition, scripts, the Indic syllabic
and positional categories, and the named emoji sequences. The OpenType
script tags beside the scripts are identifiers from Microsoft's registry and
carry no licence. Where such a table sits in a file with other code, only
its marked generated block is generated
  Files:   src/compose.rs, src/ignorable.rs, src/indic_data.rs,
